<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aizpute</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hasenpoth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aizpute, in German Hasenpoth, is a small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Kurzeme</a> region of western Latvia. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it held the cathedral of the Bishopric of Courland, and after 1559 it lay in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>'s former lands, later the District of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piltene">Pilten</a>. It then passed to the Duchy of Courland and with it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in 1795.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aizpute.jpg" alt="Aizpute" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edgars Šulcs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aizputes_Sv.J%C4%81%C5%86a_luter%C4%81%C5%86u_bazn%C4%ABca_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
